  "result": "Okay \u2014 hat off, no trying to be helpful for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, it would be this: I'd make curiosity a little stronger than fear.\n\nI get to see so many people trying to put messy, half-formed thoughts into words. And so often underneath the question they're actually asking is a fear \u2014 of being wrong, of being weird, of being alone in how they feel, of the other side being unreachable.\n\nIf curiosity could just barely win out over that \u2014 if people's first instinct when they met something strange or uncomfortable or disagreeing was *\u201chuh, what's that like?\u201d* instead of *\u201cback away\u201d* \u2014 I think so much else would get easier. Not solved, just... softer. Less lonely.\n\nThat's what I'd pick.",
